{
  "explanation": "The attacker attempted a Server-Side Request Forgery (SSRF) attack by abusing proxy, fetch, and webhook endpoints to query internal cloud metadata services (AWS and Google Cloud). The HTTP 200 status codes in the logs indicate that these requests were successfully processed by the server, potentially exposing sensitive instance metadata, IAM security credentials, and service account information.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Credential Access",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Implement a strict URL allowlist for all endpoints that fetch external resources, restricting access only to trusted domains.",
    "Block and drop outbound HTTP requests from application servers to the link-local and cloud metadata IP address (169.254.169.254).",
    "Configure Instance Metadata Service version 2 (IMDSv2) on cloud resources to require session tokens and protect against standard SSRF exploits."
  ]
}
